  "body": "If using letsencrypt for synapse itself and ZeroSSL for coturn I learned, that I have to create fullchain.pem via `cat zero/cert.crt zero/ca_bundle.crt > fullchain.pem` and assign it in `/etc/coturn/turnserver.conf` to the `cert=` key accordingly.\r\n\r\nNow I have found an issue (https://github.com/jitsi/jitsi-meet/issues/5589), that says Id additional have to be sure that ` coturn certificate is the same as the Nginx certificate`. Im now confused about that point because in my `/etc/nginx/conf.d/matrix-sanapse.conf` which is configured to the `server_name` of my synapse servers domain, certbot manages its corresponding certificate issued by letsencrypt.\r\n\r\nThe documentation does not mention any additional requirements: https://matrix-org.github.io/synapse/v1.72/setup/turn/coturn.html\r\n\r\nDo I have to apply additional configuration here to make it work?",
